From 4f07eb706aa672f286b9f05af4eec81a20007fe9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <tunguyenvanbn94@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:45:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp tr098] P5b: NSLookupDiagnostics and DNSDiagnostics, 20
 parameters

Ported from functions/tr098/nslookup_diagnostic and dns_diagnostics;
the lookups stay in nslookup_launch / dnsDiagnostics_launch.

NSLookupDiagnostics: 8 leaves + Result.{i} (5 leaves).  Result.<n> is
easycwmp.@local[<n>] of -P /var/state/nslookup_result, where the launcher
"uci add"s one section per answer; the count comes from
ResultNumberOfEntries of the parameter store.  The launcher's
"uci -P ... commit" is a no-op (uci cli.c: -P sets CLI_FLAG_NOCOMMIT), so
results never reach /etc/config.

DNSDiagnostics: 7 leaves.  DNSServer, ResultNumberOfEntries and the
Result. object are commented out in the shell (dns_diagnostics:15/18/21),
so Result.{i} was never reachable on the product; not ported.

Kept: Timeout and NumberOfRepetitions are stored unchecked and without
stopping a running lookup (nslookup_set / dnslookup_set).  Deliberate
difference: Result.{i} stops at 256 instances.

diag_mtk: diag_dns store, diag_store_value_nostop(), diag_result_get(),
diag_ifconfig_prints() moved here from traceroute_mtk.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
